Two names cxx1 emits and cl does not, both definitions nothing in this case calls: `??0Two@@QEAA@XZ`, a constructor for a class only ever built as a base subobject, and `??_DC@@QEAAXXZ`, C's vbase destructor, where no complete C is ever destroyed. cxx1 emits both beside their class rather than on demand - the same shape virtual-base-diamond.nocl records, and the same one its .nonames records against clang on the Itanium targets. No name differs. What this case measures - which constructor the most-derived class calls for a virtual base, and with what arguments - is checked by its output, which this box runs.
